    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T0OROUTC5",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-out of stage 0, copy 5 of 10: same majority(A0, B0, C0) as T0OROUT, feeding T1H2N5C2.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_3e3400654a1b4b29b271c9214beef9e6",
        "IdGuid": "a63faef5-66a6-4d23-9b51-03a864a7c90c",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "4cb5d299-2758-4eb1-8ff4-0a5f57432782",
