    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T2H1CARRYC4",
        "Description": "NOT reading (input A, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.375) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-OR copy 4 of stage 2: Y = A2 AND B2, feeding T2ORNOT1C4.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_951afa94ed0b468c85e63a0cac5cdf3e",
        "IdGuid": "2ffca233-6efe-4158-b060-2b70fc6710b0",
